## 9B. Zoneless Change Detection by Default (Angular 21, 2026 CRITICAL)

**Zoneless is now the DEFAULT in Angular 21. Zone.js is optional.**

### The Fundamental Shift

```typescript
// ANGULAR 20: Zone.js always enabled
bootstrapApplication(AppComponent, {
  providers: [provideRouter(routes)]
  // Zone.js automatically included, always running
});

// ANGULAR 21: Zoneless is default
bootstrapApplication(AppComponent, {
  providers: [
    provideRouter(routes),
    provideExperimentalZonelessChangeDetection() // Now standard!
  ]
});
```

### How It Works

```typescript
// Zone.js (OLD): Detects ALL async operations
setTimeout(() => {}, 100);      // ⚠️ Change detection triggered
Promise.resolve().then(() => {}); // ⚠️ Change detection triggered
http.get('/api').subscribe();     // ⚠️ Change detection triggered
// Result: 3 unnecessary change detection runs!

// Zoneless (NEW): Only signals trigger change detection
count = signal(0);
setTimeout(() => {
  count.set(1); // ✅ Change detection triggered ONCE
}, 100);
// Result: 1 precise change detection run!
```

### Real Performance Gains

```
Scenario: User searches while results load

Zone.js (OLD):
- Keystroke 'a' → change detection
- Keystroke 'n' → change detection  
- API starts → change detection
- Network latency (200ms) → multiple change detections
- Results arrive → change detection
- Keystroke 'g' → change detection
Total: 10+ change detection runs (some unnecessary)

Zoneless (NEW):
- Keystroke 'a' → searchTerm signal updated (1 CD)
- Keystroke 'n' → searchTerm signal updated (1 CD)
- API request starts (no CD)
- Network latency (no CD)
- Results arrive → results signal updated (1 CD)
- Keystroke 'g' → searchTerm signal updated (1 CD)
Total: 4 targeted change detection runs

🎯 Interview stat: 60-80% reduction in change detection cycles!
```

### Migration Strategy

```typescript
// Step 1: Convert services to signals
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class UserService {
  private _users = signal<User[]>([]);
  users = this._users.asReadonly();
  
  loadUsers() {
    this.http.get<User[]>('/api/users')
      .pipe(tap(users => this._users.set(users)))
      .subscribe();
  }
}

// Step 2: Update components to OnPush
@Component({
  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush
})
export class UserListComponent {
  users = inject(UserService).users;
}

// Step 3: Enable zoneless
bootstrapApplication(AppComponent, {
  providers: [
    provideRouter(routes),
    provideExperimentalZonelessChangeDetection()
  ]
});

// Step 4: Remove Zone.js workarounds
// ❌ No more: .detectChanges(), markForCheck(), changeDetectorRef
// ✅ Signals handle everything automatically
```

### Interview Zoneless Q&A

```
Q: "How does zoneless differ from Zone.js?"
A: "Zone.js intercepts ALL async operations and triggers change detection. Zoneless waits for explicit signal notifications. This is more precise: change detection only runs when actual state changes occur."

Q: "What's the catch?"
A: "Manual data mutations outside signals won't trigger change detection. Solution: always use signals for state, never mutate directly."

Q: "Should new apps use zoneless?"
A: "Absolutely, yes. It's the default in Angular 21 and the future direction. All new apps should start with zoneless enabled. It's simpler, faster, and aligns with the framework's evolution."

Q: "How to debug when UI doesn't update?"
A: "Check: 1) Using signals for state? 2) Mutating instead of setting? 3) Component is OnPush? 4) In a reactive context? Angular DevTools signals visualizer helps."
```

