## 9D. @defer Blocks and Lazy Loading (Stable in 2026)

**@defer is the modern way to lazy-load components.**

```typescript
// ❌ OLD: *ngIf hides but still creates component
@Component({
  template: `
    <div *ngIf="showChart">
      <app-heavy-chart></app-heavy-chart> <!-- Always created, just hidden -->
    </div>
  `
})

// ✅ NEW: @defer only creates when needed
@Component({
  template: `
    @defer (on viewport) {
      <app-heavy-chart></app-heavy-chart> <!-- Only created when user scrolls -->
    } @placeholder {
      <p>Chart will load when you scroll down...</p>
    } @loading {
      <p>Loading chart...</p>
    } @error {
      <p>Failed to load chart</p>
    }
  `
})
export class DashboardComponent {}

// Triggers:
// - on viewport: Load when scrolled into view
// - on interaction: Load on click/hover
// - on timer(5s): Load after 5 seconds
// - when condition(): Load when signal becomes true
```

### Real-World Impact

```
App with 20 reports/charts

OLD WAY: All 20 components created upfront
- Initial bundle: 500KB
- Time to interactive: 3 seconds

NEW WAY (@defer + lazy loading): Components created on demand
- Initial bundle: 100KB (only critical UI)
- Time to interactive: 300ms
- Reports load in background as user navigates
- Result: 5x faster initial load, better UX
```

