## 14. 2026 Angular Architecture Checklist

### ✅ Signal-based State Management
- [ ] Services use signals, not BehaviorSubject
- [ ] Forms use `model()` directive (Signal Forms)
- [ ] Computed signals for derived state
- [ ] No observable subscriptions without takeUntil/async pipe
- [ ] Signal mutations use `.set()` or `.update()`

### ✅ Zoneless Change Detection
- [ ] New apps have `provideExperimentalZonelessChangeDetection`
- [ ] Old apps have migration plan to zoneless
- [ ] No Zone.js workarounds (setTimeout, markForCheck, detectChanges)
- [ ] All state changes go through signals
- [ ] Debugging uses Angular DevTools signal visualizer

### ✅ Modern Control Flow
- [ ] All `*ngIf` replaced with `@if/@else`
- [ ] All `*ngFor` replaced with `@for` (with `track`)
- [ ] All `*ngSwitch` replaced with `@switch/@case/@default`
- [ ] Using `@defer` for non-critical components
- [ ] Lazy loading strategy for all routes

### ✅ Standalone Components & Routes
- [ ] Zero NgModule files (except legacy migration)
- [ ] All routes use `loadComponent`/`loadChildren` (lazy loading)
- [ ] Providers use `providedIn: 'root'` (tree-shakable)
- [ ] Minimal imports per component
- [ ] HttpClient, Router, etc. auto-provided at root

### ✅ Testing with Vitest
- [ ] Test suite runs with Vitest (not Karma)
- [ ] No browser global assumptions
- [ ] Signal-aware tests (effects, computed, mutations)
- [ ] Code coverage 80%+ for business logic
- [ ] No flaky tests (proper async handling)

### ✅ Security & Performance
- [ ] CSP (Content Security Policy) configured
